 {
  "name": "test_cleanup_on_a_real_repo",
  "argv": [],
  "config": "[forge]\nkind = \"github\"\nrepo = \"o/r\"\n\n[worktree_audit]\nprotected_paths = [\".port-registry\"]\n",
  "env": {},
  "setup": [
   {
    "repo": ".",
    "branch": "main"
   },
   {
    "worktree": ".claude/worktrees/issue-9-x",
    "of": ".",
    "branch": "issue-9-x"
   },
   {
    "worktree": ".claude/worktrees/feat-open",
    "of": ".",
    "branch": "feat-open"
   },
   {
    "file": ".claude/worktrees/feat-open/wip.txt",
    "text": "x"
   },
   {
    "file": ".claude/worktrees/stale-leftover/README.md",
    "text": "x"
   },
   {
    "file": ".claude/worktrees/worktrees/.port-registry",
    "text": "9=20009\n"
   }
  ],
  "forge_calls": [
   {
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/repos/o/r/pulls?state=all&per_page=100",
    "status": 200,
    "body": [
     {
      "number": 9,
      "state": "closed",
      "merged_at": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "head": {
       "ref": "issue-9-x"
      }
     },
     {
      "number": 12,
      "state": "open",
      "merged_at": null,
      "head": {
       "ref": "feat-open"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
  ],
  "expect": {
   "stdout": "| worktree | branch | PR state | unpushed commits | dirty tree | last session | live? | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| root | main | — | ? | ? | — | — | 🔒 never touch |\n| worktrees | worktrees | — | ? | ? | — | — | 🔒 never touch |\n| feat-open | feat-open | #12 open | 1 | yes | — | — | ⛔ save first |\n| issue-9-x | issue-9-x | #9 merged | 1 | no | — | — | ✅ safe to remove [squash-merge] |\n| stale-leftover | stale-leftover | — | ? | ? | — | — | ❓ orphan — manual |\n\nCommands — read the table first; this script runs nothing.\n\n```bash\ngit worktree remove \"{root}/.claude/worktrees/issue-9-x\"\n```\n```bash\ngit branch -D issue-9-x\n```\n\nPort blocks (registered in worktrees/.port-registry, read-only):\n  issue-9-x  port 20009  {root}/.claude/worktrees/issue-9-x\nThe process that actually holds the port is not looked up here — an empty list above does not mean that nothing runs.\n",
   "stderr": "",
   "code": 0
  }
 },
